[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 764,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 701,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119734,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 701,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma (B-ALL/LBL) NOS is a neoplasm of lymphoblasts of B-cell lineage that includes B-ALL/LBL cases that do not meet the criteria for any B-ALL/LBL types that are defined by defined genetic abnormalities.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 765,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 702,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119735,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 702,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>9811/3 B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma, NOS</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 766,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 703,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119736,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 703,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>2A70.0 B-lymphoblastic leukaemia or lymphoma, not elsewhere classified</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 767,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 704,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119737,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 704,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Acceptable:</em> B-cell lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma NOS; pro-B lymphoblastic leukaemia; pre-B-lymphoblastic leukaemia; pro-/pre-B-lymphoblastic leukaemia; B-cell acute lymphoblastic leukaemia.</p>\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> precursor B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma; B-cell acute lymphoid leukaemia; B-lymphoblastic lymphoma; common precursor B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma; common lymphoblastic leukaemia.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 768,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 705,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119738,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 705,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 769,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 706,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119739,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 706,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL and B-LBL represent the same disease. B-ALL always involves the bone marrow and usually also involves the peripheral blood. Extramedullary involvement is common and is by definition the primary site of involvement in B-LBL. For details, see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em> .</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 770,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 707,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119740,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 707,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 771,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 708,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119741,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 708,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Currently, B-ALL/LBL-NOS represents approximately 5&ndash;10% of all B-ALL/LBLs, excluding definitive and provisional entities {33895809; 34250504; 30487223; 30643249}. This proportion will likely decrease with the identification of additional genetic drivers.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 772,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 709,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119742,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 709,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 773,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 710,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119743,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 710,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>B-ALL/LBL development probably involves cumulative dysregulations of key regulatory pathways of self-renewal, cell proliferation, apoptosis, differentiation, and/or their signalling pathways, many of which are in common among all B-ALL/LBL subtypes, including B-ALL/LBL-NOS {25184049; 23612374; 30697448; 31367767; 32247396}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 780,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 717,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119744,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 717,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Not relevant</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 774,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 711,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119745,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 711,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 775,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 712,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119746,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 712,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 776,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 713,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119747,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 713,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>Other definitive and provisional subtypes must be excluded through cytogenetic analysis (karyotype, FISH, chromosomal microarray), genetic sequencing (RNA, DNA), and/or gene expression profiling. Molecular profiling has identified rare but recurrent genetic alterations in cases currently classified as B-ALL/LBL-NOS {33895809; 30487223; 30643249}.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 779,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 716,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119748,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 716,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> meets the diagnostic criteria for B-ALL/LBL (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/63/385\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>B-lymphoblastic leukaemia/lymphoma</em>); does not meet criteria for any defined B-ALL/LBL types after comprehensive testing.</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 777,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 714,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119749,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 714,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>No unique features</p>\r\n\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 778,
    "bookid": 63,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 715,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 119750,
        "bookId": 63,
        "chapterId": 111,
        "headingId": 715,
        "headingText": "\r\n\r\n<p>In children, the prognosis of this group is intermediate, with a 5-year event-free survival rate of 86%, and probably encompasses B-ALLs with heterogeneous clinical behaviour {34250504}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2024-03-12T09:51:10"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
